CDialogTree
{
Name=The Acid Wash
Portrait=!None
Should Have Voiceovers=0
Default Canceled Node Action=
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 the channel
Text=The floor here has been cut into a channel with a fall to the west, and the stone along the bottom is eaten shallow and smooth the way a streambed is. Steam stands in it and does not clear. High on both walls there are terraces with men on them, and the men have bows -- whatever runs down this channel, they have no intention of being in it.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 the first sluice
Text=Something lets go up-slope to the east, and the hiss arrives a good way ahead of it. The gate empties, the channel is ready again about ten seconds later, and standing still is the only mistake here that matters.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=3 the second sluice
Text=A second gate, set higher and off to the north, with a wider floor beneath it: more room for the wash to spread across, and less to stand clear on. The same ten seconds.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=4 the sluice control
Text=A switch is set into the wall at waist height here, iron, and the rock around it is worn pale by hands. Across the passage beside it a rank of spiked gates stands closed. Whoever runs the sluices runs them from this spot -- which makes this the spot where they stop.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=5 the gates open
Text=The switch gives with a sound like a coffin lid, and the hiss up the channel stops for the first time since you came in. The spiked gates beside you swing off the passage they were holding. Both sluices are dead, and the terraces above have nothing left to wait for.
Should Have Voiceover=0
}
